# Pretty Chitty Project Guidelines

## Project Structure
- This is a React + TypeScript game engine library
- Components are in `src/library/components/`
- Hooks are in `src/library/hooks/`
- Game logic is in `src/library/game/`
- Rendering logic is in `src/library/rendering/`

## Code Style
- Use functional React components (not class components)
- Prefer hooks over class-based patterns
- Use TypeScript strictly - avoid `any` types when possible
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- JSX files need to `import React from "react";` at the top (plus other hooks, if necessary)
- I hate loops or if statements that don't use braces `{}` - always use braces for clarity



## File Organization
- New hooks should go in `src/library/hooks/` (not inline in component files)
- Context definitions and custom hooks should be separate files
- Components that are tightly related to panels should go in `src/library/components/Panel/`

## Testing
- Run `yarn build` to verify TypeScript compilation and build the project
- The build process includes documentation generation and webpack bundling

## Important Patterns
- Components use MUI (Material-UI) for styling with the `sx` prop
- The project uses a custom theme system via `useGameTheme()`
- Game state is managed through event channels and custom hooks
- WebGL rendering is handled through Three.js

## What to Avoid
- Don't add emoji unless explicitly requested
- Don't create markdown documentation files unless asked
- Don't use `React.` prefix for hooks (import them directly)
